The Conjuring: The Devil Made Me Do It is a 2021 American supernatural horror film directed by Michael Chaves, with
a screenplay by David Leslie Johnson-McGoldrick from a story by Johnson-McGoldrick and James Wan.

13
00:51:32,142 --> 00:51:38,142
The film is a sequel to The Conjuring (2013) and The Conjuring 2 (2016),
and the seventh installment in The Conjuring Universe.

14
00:55:30,000 --> 00:55:36,000
Patrick Wilson and Vera Farmiga reprise their roles as paranormal investigators and authors Ed and Lorraine Warren,
with Ruairi O'Connor, Sarah Catherine Hook in her feature film debut, and Julian Hilliard also starring.

15
00:59:27,857 --> 00:59:33,857
Wan and Peter Safran return to produce the film, which is based on the trial of Arne Cheyenne Johnson, a murder trial that took
place in 1981 Connecticut, in addition to The Devil in Connecticut, a book about the trial written by Gerald Brittle.

16
01:03:25,714 --> 01:03:31,714
Initial development for a third Conjuring film began in 2016, though Wan stated that he would not be
directing another film in the series due to scheduling conflicts with other projects.

17
01:07:23,571 --> 01:07:29,571
Safran confirmed that the next film would not be a haunted house film.

18
01:11:21,428 --> 01:11:27,428
By June 2017, it was officially announced that a third installment was in
development, with David Leslie Johnson hired to write the screenplay.

19
01:15:19,285 --> 01:15:25,285
Michael Chaves was announced as the film's director, after
previously directing The Curse of La Llorona (2019).

20
01:19:17,142 --> 01:19:23,142
Filming took place in Georgia in mid-2019.

21
01:23:15,000 --> 01:23:21,000
Originally slated for a September 2020 release, the film
was delayed due to the COVID-19 pandemic.

22
